  "2026-10-21T18:55:52.588Z",codex-agent,"author=codex-agent,\"text=Authorized tracker reconciliation, audit 2026-10-21. Reverified current main 765b440ce656: canonical pmc-xndl exists and audit overlap remains unchanged; source tree exactly matches the audited snapshot. **Track published pm-github apply-path limitations exposed by certification review.** Canonical id: pmc-xndl in pm-changelog. Both consumer reports enumerate the same five pm-github export/project apply-path limitations; fixes belong in pm-github, not separate standup implementation. Canonical item: pmc-xndl (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pmc-xndl.toon).\""
  "2026-10-22T11:17:12.443Z",codex-agent,"Review evidence clarification for PR #141: this consumer description originally lists three apply-path limitations (cancellation omission, repeat-export duplicates and project-draft duplication). All three are covered by the five limitations in canonical pmc-xndl, whose current status is open. The duplicate closure and release association record tracking consolidation only; they do not claim upstream fixes or synthetic write-path acceptance. Earlier comments remain in append-only history."
